(5008733, 728860, 30861, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kaiser_chief:</b></div><hr/><i> The Post Processing of this photo does not work for me.  Would have preferred to see the shot in colour as a more standard presentation </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I love this comment, because the image is literally straight from the camera, no post processing aside from a slight crop, and in full color as the camera saw it, shooting straight into the sun...</td>', 'Originally posted by kaiser_chief: The Post Processing of this photo does not work for me.  Would have preferred to see the shot in colour as a more standard presentation   I love this comment, because the image is literally straight from the camera, no post processing aside from a slight crop, and in full color as the camera saw it, shooting straight into the sun...', '2008-10-15 01:10:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5008737, 728589, 67697, '<td valign="top">Wow, you moved!  That is quite a jump in locales.  Nary a building or bike or car or harajuku girl in sight in this photo :D.  Look forward to seeing more pics from your new home!</td>', 'Wow, you moved!  That is quite a jump in locales.  Nary a building or bike or car or harajuku girl in sight in this photo :D.  Look forward to seeing more pics from your new home!', '2008-10-15 01:11:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5008739, 728831, 54645, '<td valign="top">Great image, I find it underrated, at least based on my tastes! I disagree with you in that the color would have scored better. Who cares! The sepia tone tugs at the heart; makes me yearn for the childhood summer days spent at the beach. Growing up in Southern California, that was nearly every day! As a point of critique, I feel that you could have made a bigger impact with a stronger composition, specifically the sky. I find myself scrolling down to "crop" some of the sky out. Still a successful image because it spoke to at least one viewer, and that was before I read the title!</td>', 'Great image, I find it underrated, at least based on my tastes! I disagree with you in that the color would have scored better. Who cares! The sepia tone tugs at the heart; makes me yearn for the childhood summer days spent at the beach. Growing up in Southern California, that was nearly every day! As a point of critique, I feel that you could have made a bigger impact with a stronger composition, specifically the sky. I find myself scrolling down to "crop" some of the sky out. Still a successful image because it spoke to at least one viewer, and that was before I read the title!', '2008-10-15 01:11:51.000000', NULL, 0),
