(5009512, 729255, 28853, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments... I know it wasn''t a great score but I enjoyed to participate in my first challenge... I''ll take advice from all of you<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dancindiva5105:</b></div><hr/><i> why is this in past tense? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually this is a game I liked to play a lot when I was a kid, so I was aiming to share the idea of something old, memories from youth, forgotten happyness... things like that... hence the title, sepia and the playground as background...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-10-15 10:18:50.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the comments... I know it wasn''t a great score but I enjoyed to participate in my first challenge... I''ll take advice from all of you Originally posted by dancindiva5105: why is this in past tense?   Actually this is a game I liked to play a lot when I was a kid, so I was aiming to share the idea of something old, memories from youth, forgotten happyness... things like that... hence the title, sepia and the playground as background...', '2008-10-15 11:17:22.000000', '2008-10-15 11:18:50.000000', 0),
(5009513, 727497, 53170, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments, folks, I shall try and improve in the future.<br/> <br/>The capture could sure use some work, especially about the background, as rightly mentioned.<br/>Maybe I should have tried climbing up the lights hanging directly above the table to capture the shot against the original background.<br/>About the vertical line, whenever I take a photo with ISO higher than 100, that line comes.<br/> <br/>I have an S5IS by Canon (re-quoted for ready reference). Any ideas on what the problem is?</td>', 'Thanks for the comments, folks, I shall try and improve in the future. The capture could sure use some work, especially about the background, as rightly mentioned.Maybe I should have tried climbing up the lights hanging directly above the table to capture the shot against the original background.About the vertical line, whenever I take a photo with ISO higher than 100, that line comes. I have an S5IS by Canon (re-quoted for ready reference). Any ideas on what the problem is?', '2008-10-15 11:17:28.000000', NULL, 0),
