(5016748, 728165, 80096, '<td valign="top">Hey Joe! I didn''t see this when I voted but I like what you tried to do here. I think you missed the boat on the title/theme but overall it''s a very interesting shot with unique shadowing and tones. It has a definite mood but more along the lines of night moves or after hours. It''s a shame you didn''t focus more on the partiers. I know you''ll do much better next time, this was only a temporary setback and a very small one. I do like it though. ;-)</td>', 'Hey Joe! I didn''t see this when I voted but I like what you tried to do here. I think you missed the boat on the title/theme but overall it''s a very interesting shot with unique shadowing and tones. It has a definite mood but more along the lines of night moves or after hours. It''s a shame you didn''t focus more on the partiers. I know you''ll do much better next time, this was only a temporary setback and a very small one. I do like it though. ;-)', '2008-10-20 17:55:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5017355, 729263, 88136, '<td valign="top">hey thats pretty cool. looks like it could be a cd cover or something like that</td>', 'hey thats pretty cool. looks like it could be a cd cover or something like that', '2008-10-21 00:18:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5017531, 729286, 51793, '<td valign="top">I thought about heading downtown to get some pictures of this place, but I''m waiting on a friend to give me a call about it first. The guy that prints my shirts is going pro next year and he skates down there all the time. <br/> <br/>As far as this picture I think there is a lot going on in the background. Maybe a different angle to make the background more of the bowl than people getting into their car. The colors look good and the processing is good but the background doesn''t do it for me. <br/> <br/>I like the boarder but I think it''s a bit thick. <br/> <br/>Anyway 5.7261 isn''t bad for someone trying to get back into the swing of things.</td>', 'I thought about heading downtown to get some pictures of this place, but I''m waiting on a friend to give me a call about it first. The guy that prints my shirts is going pro next year and he skates down there all the time.  As far as this picture I think there is a lot going on in the background. Maybe a different angle to make the background more of the bowl than people getting into their car. The colors look good and the processing is good but the background doesn''t do it for me.  I like the boarder but I think it''s a bit thick.  Anyway 5.7261 isn''t bad for someone trying to get back into the swing of things.', '2008-10-21 07:19:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5017750, 728459, 95687, '<td valign="top">this is terrific work and completely underrated</td>', 'this is terrific work and completely underrated', '2008-10-21 11:26:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5018561, 729277, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>What a beautiful little girl.  I really like the natural expression on her face.<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I like that her face and the drawing somewhat balance each other without one overpowering the other.  It might be a bit stronger if her body and the drawing formed more of an angle in the frame rather than a straight-ish line, but it still seems very well balanced.  The crop feels a touch tight to me.  Maybe if just a touch was shaved off of the top, or if there were more space on the left it would open things up a bit.<br/> <br/>Technically, it is well focused and well-exposed.  The critical details are visible without blowing anything or losing details anywhere.  It feels a touch flat to me, but that may be from the dominance of the pavement she is on.  Maybe a touch more contrast or shadows/highlights could help alleviate the flatness.<br/> <br/>Overall, a good shot that meets the challenge in a relaxing, pleasant way.<br/> <br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat What a beautiful little girl.  I really like the natural expression on her face. Compositionally, I like that her face and the drawing somewhat balance each other without one overpowering the other.  It might be a bit stronger if her body and the drawing formed more of an angle in the frame rather than a straight-ish line, but it still seems very well balanced.  The crop feels a touch tight to me.  Maybe if just a touch was shaved off of the top, or if there were more space on the left it would open things up a bit. Technically, it is well focused and well-exposed.  The critical details are visible without blowing anything or losing details anywhere.  It feels a touch flat to me, but that may be from the dominance of the pavement she is on.  Maybe a touch more contrast or shadows/highlights could help alleviate the flatness. Overall, a good shot that meets the challenge in a relaxing, pleasant way. Karma', '2008-10-21 16:32:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5018684, 729116, 66384, '<td valign="top">The image certainly has happy colors. I think it''s a wonderful photo. A bit if a stretch for play, since my impression of spiders is that it''s all work, but I do love the bright image.</td>', 'The image certainly has happy colors. I think it''s a wonderful photo. A bit if a stretch for play, since my impression of spiders is that it''s all work, but I do love the bright image.', '2008-10-21 17:45:05.000000', NULL, 0),
